meta {
  name: Get Ecatalog by ID
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/ecatalogs/6a38f615c3d65a5f868b1a41
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.pdf_active: eq false
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 and 2026-09-21. Fetches the pre-existing "Plytix Brand
  Portal" ecatalog by id -- read-only fixture, never mutated (no undeclared
  `PATCH`/`DELETE` spot-check attempted here, unlike every create-able resource in
  this project, per the ground rule against mutating pre-existing account data).

  Subpath discovery (`GET .../bogus_xyz`) raw field list: `['id','account_id','name',
  'logo','product_list_id','asset_list_id','output_attributes','assets','settings',
  'is_public','password_required','data_sheet_active','pds_active','pdf_active',
  'quote_active','specification_sheet_active','price_list_active','pds_template_id',
  'price_list_id','specification_sheet_id','pdf_catalog_id','exportable_attributes',
  'password','notification_list','quote_request_output_attributes',
  'notification_active','created','modified']` -- matches the spec's
  `ECatalogCreateInputDto` field names closely, plus output-only fields (`is_public`,
  `assets`, `created`).

  `pdf_active: false` confirms this ecatalog doesn't use the (feature-gated-off) PDF
  catalog integration either.
}

example {
  name: 200 - Full Parameters (All Fields, Nested Entries)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-22 against the "Plytix Brand Portal" ecatalog. Every top-level field is shown untruncated (unlike the "Top-Level Fields Only" example above, which omits output_attributes/assets/settings entirely) -- output_attributes/assets/settings' larger arrays are trimmed to one representative entry per distinct shape (noted inline via _*_note keys, NOT real API fields) since the full arrays run 30+ entries. Staff email addresses in notification_list were redacted to teammate1@example.com/teammate2@example.com; every other value is verbatim. New finding: this single-resource GET returns created: null, differing from the List example below (and the older "Top-Level Fields Only" example's placeholder date) -- worth flagging as a possible field-population gap on this resource.

